<title>SWITZERLAND: ABB AB raises 1996 dividend.</title>
<headline>ABB AB raises 1996 dividend.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calender 1996 vs 1995</p>
<p>				  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Dividend (crowns per share) 17.50	    vs 16.00</p>
<p> Net income			4,144	    vs 4,682</p>
<p> Net per share, crowns	 44.20	    vs 49.90</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name is ABB AB, formerly known as Asea AB. ABB AB is a holding company whose main assets is its 50 percent in ABB Asea Brown Boveri AG. The other 50 percent of ABB is owned by Switzerland's ABB AG.  </p>
<p>ABB said its board of directors would propose to the 1997 annual general meeting that ABB's A and B shares are split 10-for-one, lowering the par value of the shares to 5.0 Swedish crowns from 50.</p>
<p>Each old share has the right to 10 new shares of the same class. Trading in the new shares is expected to start April 21, 1997. -- Peter Nielsen, Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
